</script></head><body><div id="main"><div style="display: none"><a href="/pdfs/bedrock-agentcore/latest/devguide/bedrock-agentcore-dg.pdf#web-search-api-reference" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="Open PDF"></a></div><div id="breadcrumbs" class="breadcrumb"><a href="/index.html">Documentation</a><a href="/bedrock-agentcore/index.html">Amazon Bedrock AgentCore</a><a href="what-is-bedrock-agentcore.html">Developer Guide</a></div><div id="page-toc-src"><a href="#web-search-api-request">Request fields</a><a href="#web-search-api-response">Response</a></div><div id="main-content" class="awsui-util-container"><div id="main-col-body"><awsdocs-language-banner data-service="$ctrl.pageService"></awsdocs-language-banner><h1 class="topictitle" id="web-search-api-reference">AgentCore Web Search request and response</h1><div class="awsdocs-page-header-container"><awsdocs-page-header></awsdocs-page-header><awsdocs-filter-selector id="awsdocs-filter-selector"></awsdocs-filter-selector></div><p>This page describes the fields of an <code class="code">InvokeWebSearch</code> request, the rules that the API applies to them, and the response.</p>
      <h2 id="web-search-api-request">Request fields</h2>
      <p>You call the API on the Amazon Bedrock AgentCore data plane endpoint, for example <code class="code">bedrock-agentcore.us-east-1.amazonaws.com</code>. The AWS SDKs and the AWS Command Line Interface (AWS CLI) sign each request for you with AWS Signature Version 4 (SigV4) for the service name <code class="code">bedrock-agentcore</code>.</p>
      <div class="table-container"><div class="table-contents"><table id="d0e1"><thead>
               <tr>
                  <th align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;">Field</th>
                  <th align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;">Type</th>
                  <th align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;">Required</th>
                  <th align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;">Description</th>
               </tr>
            </thead>
               <tr>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>
                        <code class="code">webSearchId</code>
                     </p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>string</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>Yes</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>The identifier of the web search tool to invoke. The AWS managed web search tool is <code class="code">web-search.v1</code>. The request sends this value in the URI path.</p>
                  </td>
               </tr>
               <tr>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>
                        <code class="code">searchQuery</code>
                     </p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>string</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>Yes</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>The text to search for. The text must be 1–200 characters long.</p>
                  </td>
               </tr>
               <tr>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>
                        <code class="code">maxResults</code>
                     </p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>integer</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>No</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>The maximum number of results to return, from 1 to 25. If you don’t specify a value, the API returns up to 25 results.</p>
                  </td>
               </tr>
               <tr>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>
                        <code class="code">filters</code>
                     </p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>object</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>No</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>The filters that narrow the results. The object can contain <code class="code">domainFilter</code>, <code class="code">publishedDateFilter</code>, or both.</p>
                  </td>
               </tr>
               <tr>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>
                        <code class="code">filters.domainFilter.include</code>
                     </p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>array of strings</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>No</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>The domains to return results from. The API doesn’t return results from other domains. The list holds 1–100 domain names.</p>
                  </td>
               </tr>
               <tr>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>
                        <code class="code">filters.domainFilter.exclude</code>
                     </p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>array of strings</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>No</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>The domains that the API never returns results from. The list holds 1–100 domain names.</p>
                  </td>
               </tr>
               <tr>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>
                        <code class="code">filters.publishedDateFilter.publishedAfter</code>
                     </p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>timestamp</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>No</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>The start of the publication time range, inclusive. The API returns only results published at or after this time. For example, <code class="code">2026-01-01T00:00:00Z</code>.</p>
                  </td>
               </tr>
               <tr>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>
                        <code class="code">filters.publishedDateFilter.publishedBefore</code>
                     </p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>timestamp</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>No</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>The end of the publication time range, inclusive. The API returns only results published at or before this time. For example, <code class="code">2026-01-31T23:59:59Z</code>.</p>
                  </td>
               </tr>
            </table></div></div>
      <p>The API applies the following rules to the request:</p>
      <div class="itemizedlist">
          
          
          
          
      <ul class="itemizedlist"><li class="listitem">
            <p>
               <strong>Domain names</strong> – Specify a domain name only, such as <code class="code">example.net</code>, without a scheme or a path. A root domain also matches its subdomains. For example, <code class="code">example.net</code> also matches <code class="code">docs.example.net</code>. You can specify <code class="code">include</code>, <code class="code">exclude</code>, or both. Each domain name can be up to 253 characters long.</p>
         </li><li class="listitem">
            <p>
               <strong>Publication times</strong> – Each value is a timestamp. The AWS SDKs and the AWS CLI send it as a date-time in Coordinated Universal Time (UTC), for example <code class="code">2026-01-01T00:00:00Z</code>. If you pass a date without a time, such as <code class="code">2026-01-01</code> to the AWS CLI, it means midnight UTC at the start of that day. To include a whole day in <code class="code">publishedBefore</code>, use the last second of that day, for example <code class="code">2026-01-31T23:59:59Z</code>. You can specify <code class="code">publishedAfter</code>, <code class="code">publishedBefore</code>, or both. If <code class="code">publishedAfter</code> is later than <code class="code">publishedBefore</code>, the request fails with a <code class="code">ValidationException</code>.</p>
         </li><li class="listitem">
            <p>
               <strong>Other fields</strong> – The request body can contain only <code class="code">searchQuery</code>, <code class="code">maxResults</code>, and <code class="code">filters</code>. The API rejects a request that contains any other top-level field with a <code class="code">ValidationException</code>.</p>
         </li><li class="listitem">
            <p>
               <strong>Body size</strong> – The request body can be up to 32 KiB.</p>
         </li></ul></div>
    
      <h2 id="web-search-api-response">Response</h2>
      <p>The response contains a <code class="code">results</code> array with the search results, in ranked order. The API doesn’t paginate. It returns up to <code class="code">maxResults</code> results in a single response, and it can return fewer.</p>
      <p>Each result contains the following fields:</p>
      <div class="table-container"><div class="table-contents"><table id="d0e2"><thead>
               <tr>
                  <th align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;">Field</th>
                  <th align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;">Type</th>
                  <th align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;">Always present</th>
                  <th align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;">Description</th>
               </tr>
            </thead>
               <tr>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>
                        <code class="code">text</code>
                     </p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>string</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>Yes</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>A text extract from the page.</p>
                  </td>
               </tr>
               <tr>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>
                        <code class="code">title</code>
                     </p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>string</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>No</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>The title of the page.</p>
                  </td>
               </tr>
               <tr>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>
                        <code class="code">url</code>
                     </p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>string</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>No</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>The URL of the page.</p>
                  </td>
               </tr>
               <tr>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>
                        <code class="code">publishedAt</code>
                     </p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>timestamp</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>No</p>
                  </td>
                  <td align="left" style="text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" tabindex="-1">
                     <p>The time the page was published. The API omits this field when the publication time isn’t known.</p>
                  </td>
               </tr>
            </table></div></div>
      <p>The following example shows a response body with one result:</p>
      <pre class="programlisting"><div class="code-btn-container"><div class="btn-copy-code" title="Copy"><awsui-icon name="copy"></awsui-icon></div></div><!--DEBUG: cli (json)--><code class="json "><span>{</span>
    "results": [
        <span>{</span>
            "title": "Release highlights",
            "url": "https://docs.example.net/releases/highlights",
            "text": "The January release adds support for scheduled reports and improves search performance...",
            "publishedAt": "2026-01-15T17:00:00Z"
        }
    ]
}</code></pre>
      <p>For the errors that the API returns, see <a href="./web-search-api-troubleshooting.html#web-search-api-errors">Troubleshoot AgentCore Web Search</a>.</p>
